{
  "_README": [
    "Hand-authored motion for the Tripo pets (the Drowned Village's five and",
    "Bogheart Caverns' eight): one static mesh each, no rig, no clips of their own.",
    "`python -I tools/pet_motions.py` turns this into Config/ModelClips/<Pet>.",
    "",
    "Each pet is a single part named Body, so these move the whole animal:",
    "position, rotation and scale. A limb cannot move on its own here -- that",
    "needs a jointed Claude Design rebuild (docs/PETS-DROWNED.md).",
    "",
    "Units: position in import studs (each pet is about 1 stud tall at import,",
    "and Fx/ModelAnimator scales the motion with the pet). Rotation in degrees",
    "as [x, y, z]. Scale as a multiplier per axis. Times in seconds.",
    "",
    "Keep the first and last key of a looping clip identical or it will jump."
  ],

